WEBVTT

00:00.499 --> 00:03.366
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.961 --> 00:07.229
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.264 --> 00:10.799
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.834 --> 00:13.802
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.837 --> 00:17.305
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.341 --> 00:20.609
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.644 --> 00:22.177
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.212 --> 00:23.545
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.580 --> 00:25.096
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.123 --> 00:34.556
Live from New York City,

00:34.591 --> 00:37.692
it's the JCPenney
Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:37.728 --> 00:39.294
The JCPenney parade?

00:39.329 --> 00:40.962
Yeah, it's like
the Macy's parade,

00:40.998 --> 00:43.231
only without
licensed characters.

00:43.267 --> 00:46.234
With the popular
balloons we all know and love--

00:46.270 --> 00:47.602
Mickey Rabbit,

00:47.638 --> 00:48.937
Sponge Cow,

00:48.972 --> 00:51.907
and Clifton the Small Blue Dog.

00:51.942 --> 00:54.776
Peter, get in here!

00:54.811 --> 00:56.378
You want to tell me
what the hell happened

00:56.413 --> 00:57.913
to our Thanksgiving turkey?

00:57.948 --> 00:59.314
Oh, that.

00:59.349 --> 01:01.183
Uh, well, last night,
Brian and I

01:01.218 --> 01:02.817
got drunk and
ate the turkey.

01:02.853 --> 01:06.087
But before you get mad,
we also ate the salad.

01:06.123 --> 01:07.756
Damn it, how could
you guys do that?!

01:07.791 --> 01:09.424
Boy, I must have
been really drunk.

01:09.459 --> 01:10.592
I don't remember
any of that.

01:10.627 --> 01:11.660
No problem.

01:11.695 --> 01:13.461
Instagram
remembers for you.

01:20.504 --> 01:22.224
Peter, we've got a houseful
of people coming

01:22.239 --> 01:24.005
and they're
expecting a turkey.

01:24.041 --> 01:25.340
Well, if they're
expecting a turkey,

01:25.375 --> 01:27.309
<i>I'll just put on
Evan Almighty for them.</i>

01:27.344 --> 01:28.344
Zap!

01:30.447 --> 01:32.948
You and Brian better get
another turkey right now!

01:32.983 --> 01:35.250
And don't bother
coming back until you do!

01:35.285 --> 01:36.551
Don't worry, Lois.
We will.

01:36.587 --> 01:37.919
Yeah, we'll be back
with a turkey

01:37.955 --> 01:39.688
faster than you can
say, "Jack Robinson."

01:39.723 --> 01:41.289
Jack Rober...

01:42.826 --> 01:45.794
Jack Row...

01:45.829 --> 01:47.696
She had a stroke that killed
the part of her brain

01:47.731 --> 01:49.397
that says "Jack Robinson."

01:49.433 --> 01:50.966
We got plenty of time.

01:55.639 --> 01:57.405
All right, Brian,
first order of business--

01:57.441 --> 01:59.307
we have to decide
who gets to ride in the cart

01:59.343 --> 02:00.709
and who has to push it.

02:00.744 --> 02:02.077
Well, I'm smaller, so...

02:02.112 --> 02:03.778
The decision
has been made.

02:03.814 --> 02:05.413
Ooh, now I want that one.

02:08.719 --> 02:11.353
Aw, crap-- looks like
they're completely sold out.

02:11.388 --> 02:12.520
Yeah, sorry.

02:12.556 --> 02:14.789
We just sold our last
turkey to that guy.

02:16.226 --> 02:19.294
You are the turkey
I have chosen to pardon.

02:19.329 --> 02:21.663
Fly free, turkey!

02:25.102 --> 02:27.469
Oh, Fudgsicles!

02:30.107 --> 02:32.307
Hey, you don't sell
turkeys here, do you?

02:32.342 --> 02:35.076
We've been to every grocery
store in town with no luck.

02:36.847 --> 02:38.613
are these little packets
of weird vitamins

02:38.649 --> 02:41.383
that vaguely suggest
they help you in the bedroom.

02:41.418 --> 02:44.753
"Performance and
stamina, for men."

02:44.788 --> 02:48.456
I know what that means.

02:52.462 --> 02:54.896
Peter, enough.
Come to bed.

02:54.931 --> 02:56.131
Uh-uh, Lois.

02:56.166 --> 02:58.333
The packet says I got to
play till I'm raw.

03:02.773 --> 03:04.072
Can't believe
every turkey

03:04.107 --> 03:06.841
within a 60-mile radius
of Quahog is sold out.

03:06.877 --> 03:09.010
I know. And now
we're so far from home,

03:09.046 --> 03:10.845
none of your
stations even work.

03:14.885 --> 03:17.419
♪ She thinks I'm beautiful ♪

03:17.454 --> 03:19.387
♪ Meet Virginia ♪

03:19.423 --> 03:21.589
Is this...
Is this fine?

03:21.625 --> 03:22.857
I mean, it's
not... it's...

03:22.893 --> 03:24.626
Yeah, it's fine if
you think it's fine.

03:24.661 --> 03:26.928
It's not that good
of a song, but we know it.

03:26.963 --> 03:28.330
Yeah, okay. Sure.

03:28.365 --> 03:29.531
♪ She never compromises... ♪

03:29.566 --> 03:30.899
Brian, I love Train.

03:30.934 --> 03:33.101
I  love Train.

03:35.372 --> 03:37.472
Chris, are Brian and
your father back yet?

03:37.507 --> 03:40.909
No. And why are you saying
the dog's name before Dad's?

03:40.944 --> 03:43.278
It's weird.
That is weird, you're right.

03:43.313 --> 03:44.612
Well, they better
get here soon.

03:44.648 --> 03:47.582
I can't host this
Thanksgiving dinner on my own.

03:47.617 --> 03:49.384
Hear that?
This thing's all on you.

03:49.419 --> 03:51.152
What? What are you
talking about?

03:51.188 --> 03:53.228
Well, the fat man's never
going to get back in time,

03:53.256 --> 03:55.790
and with him gone, that makes
you the man of the house.

03:55.826 --> 03:57.892
I sentence you to death!

03:57.928 --> 03:58.960
Chris, Chris, slow down.

03:58.995 --> 04:00.562
I'm just saying,
without Peter here,

04:00.597 --> 04:02.697
you're going to have to be
the host of Thanksgiving.

04:02.733 --> 04:05.734
You have to do everything
the fat man normally would.

04:05.769 --> 04:07.535
You mean, like,
fall asleep on the toilet

04:07.571 --> 04:10.472
and have a big red ring
on my bum for a week?

04:10.507 --> 04:12.273
No, no, no-- greeting
guests as they arrive.

04:12.309 --> 04:13.875
Facilitating small talk.

04:13.910 --> 04:16.077
And, of course, giving
the Thanksgiving toast.

04:16.113 --> 04:18.213
Boy, yesterday I'm
microwaving a cat,

04:18.248 --> 04:19.848
today I'm giving
a speech.

04:19.883 --> 04:22.817
Things move fast
around here.

04:26.323 --> 04:28.656
Hi, do you have any turkeys?

04:28.692 --> 04:30.525
Sure do.
You're looking at one.

04:30.560 --> 04:31.726
I'm sorry.

04:31.762 --> 04:34.129
You have to know me
to know I'm just joking.

04:34.164 --> 04:35.797
Sir, the day we've had,

04:35.832 --> 04:38.767
we could use
a good chuckle like that.

04:38.802 --> 04:40.168
You folks are in luck.

04:40.203 --> 04:42.470
Looks like we have
one turkey left.

04:42.506 --> 04:43.772
Oh, thank God.

04:43.807 --> 04:44.906
Oh, you're telling me.

04:44.941 --> 04:46.541
We didn't come back
with a turkey,

04:46.576 --> 04:49.010
Lois would be madder than
that time she got a Capp smear.

04:49.045 --> 04:51.346
All right, we're just going
to take a quick Capp smear.

04:51.381 --> 04:53.047
Don't you mean
pap smear?

04:53.083 --> 04:55.283
No, at this hospital
we obtain the sample

04:55.318 --> 04:58.520
using beloved British comic
strip roustabout Andy Capp.

04:58.555 --> 05:00.755
'Ello, luv.

05:00.791 --> 05:02.023
Let's have a smear.

05:02.058 --> 05:03.591
I'm not letting
you do that.

05:03.627 --> 05:04.826
You can't even see.

05:04.861 --> 05:08.930
That's all right, bird.
I goes by smell.

05:11.835 --> 05:14.636
Brian, look,
an eight-foot basket.

05:14.671 --> 05:16.070
Let me just dunk
the turkey once.

05:16.106 --> 05:18.006
I know I can jam it.

05:20.243 --> 05:21.943
That's not
a regulation rim.

05:21.978 --> 05:23.711
Okay, you know what?
I'm in charge of the turkey.

05:23.747 --> 05:25.647
You're driving.

05:30.487 --> 05:31.986
This thing on?

05:32.022 --> 05:33.054
Yes.

05:33.089 --> 05:34.322
It's not making
any noise.

05:34.357 --> 05:35.924
It's a hybrid.
Trust me, it's on.

05:35.959 --> 05:37.192
No, it's not. See?

05:51.441 --> 05:53.475
Oh, my God!

06:06.957 --> 06:09.591
Not now! Not like this!

06:15.232 --> 06:16.965
Peter, what the hell?!

06:17.000 --> 06:18.800
You chose
a turkey over me?!

06:18.835 --> 06:20.168
I almost died!

06:20.203 --> 06:23.905
I swear to God, I thought
dogs could breathe underwater.

06:29.019 --> 06:31.520
Great. The water completely
killed my phone.

06:31.555 --> 06:32.721
Oh, horrors.

06:32.756 --> 06:34.122
You have to spend
time with me

06:34.157 --> 06:35.557
without looking
at your phone.

06:35.592 --> 06:36.658
Here, give me yours.

06:36.693 --> 06:38.660
I threw mine
at a duck.

06:38.695 --> 06:40.495
Excuse me, can you help us?

06:40.531 --> 06:41.997
We're trying to get
back to Quahog.

06:42.032 --> 06:44.566
If you want, I can take you
as far as the bus station.

06:44.601 --> 06:46.201
You can?
Oh, thank you so much!

06:46.236 --> 06:48.637
Oh, that is the nicest thing
anyone's done for me

06:48.672 --> 06:51.640
since my kids gave me
that Father's Day gift.

06:51.675 --> 06:53.975
Oh, look, a tie.
Perfect.

06:57.180 --> 07:00.348
It's from all of us!

07:04.454 --> 07:06.021
All right, Chris,
acting as host

07:06.056 --> 07:08.123
will demand a higher
level of conversation.

07:08.158 --> 07:09.658
I suggest
as your opener--

07:09.693 --> 07:11.893
"Lois, everything
is delicious."

07:11.929 --> 07:13.862
Then that's
what I will say.

07:13.897 --> 07:15.730
Unless Slender Man
commands me

07:15.766 --> 07:17.265
to say something else.

07:17.301 --> 07:20.669
Ugh, this is gonna be
a bigger disaster than Y2-Gay.

07:20.704 --> 07:23.505
Three! Two! One!

07:23.540 --> 07:27.275
I hope my dad's
not watching ABC!

07:30.480 --> 07:33.114
Oh, thank God
we got on this bus.

07:33.150 --> 07:34.616
I really had to poop.

07:34.651 --> 07:36.418
Wait, where is there
a bathroom on this bus?

07:36.453 --> 07:37.852
I didn't say there
was a bathroom,

07:37.888 --> 07:39.187
I just said
I had to poop.

07:39.222 --> 07:40.422
Oh, my God!

07:40.457 --> 07:42.657
This is gross
even for a bus!

07:45.896 --> 07:47.395
I don't know what
they were so mad about,

07:47.431 --> 07:48.930
I did it in
a Rite Aid bag.

07:48.966 --> 07:50.799
Damn it, Peter!
That was our only way home!

07:50.834 --> 07:53.134
Well, that's where
you're wrong, Brian.

07:53.170 --> 07:54.736
Free bus bike!

07:54.771 --> 07:57.205
Aw, crap, this
is a girl's bike.

07:57.240 --> 07:58.506
All right,
we'll ride it,

07:58.542 --> 08:00.475
but pray to God nobody
from school sees us.

08:00.510 --> 08:02.177
Nice bike, butt-munch!

08:02.212 --> 08:05.547
Shut up!
I'm telling Miss Baumbakis!

08:09.119 --> 08:10.452
Up next on Nickelodeon,

08:10.487 --> 08:13.355
<i>Uncomfortably Hot
Eighteen-Year-Old Girls.</i>

08:13.390 --> 08:15.290
Honey, where
are you off to?

08:15.325 --> 08:16.491
To the car wash

08:16.526 --> 08:18.259
to raise money for our
new soccer uniforms.

08:18.295 --> 08:20.261
Okay, have fun.

08:20.297 --> 08:22.497
Nickelodeon--
casually ask your daughter

08:22.532 --> 08:23.898
what that girl's name is,

08:23.934 --> 08:26.368
then take your laptop
into the bathroom.

08:29.406 --> 08:31.773
Uh, Mom! Daddy!
You're right on time!

08:31.808 --> 08:34.142
Happy Thanksgiving,
dear!

08:34.177 --> 08:35.543
We brought some wine,

08:35.579 --> 08:37.879
but it's good wine
so it's just or us.

08:39.116 --> 08:41.850
Damn it. Where the hell
are they with that turkey?

08:43.887 --> 08:45.954
Hi, you've reached Brian Griffin

08:45.989 --> 08:48.156
of The Write Stuff
writing classes...

08:48.191 --> 08:49.924
Oh, God.

08:52.963 --> 08:54.295
Come on,
keep pedaling.

08:54.331 --> 08:56.064
Dinner starts in an hour.

09:01.405 --> 09:02.804
Oh! Ow!

09:02.839 --> 09:03.872
Damn it, Peter!

09:03.907 --> 09:05.006
Oh, great.

09:05.042 --> 09:06.941
You broke the chain
and now we have to walk!

09:06.977 --> 09:08.943
Unless we hitchhike.

09:08.979 --> 09:11.146
Hitchhike? You know
how dangerous that is?

09:11.181 --> 09:12.647
Besides, we're in
the middle of nowhere.

09:12.683 --> 09:14.249
There aren't even
any cars around.

09:14.284 --> 09:15.750
There's one.

09:15.786 --> 09:18.319
Hey! Hey, stop!
Give us a ride!

09:18.355 --> 09:20.822
It's just me and my upright dog.

09:20.857 --> 09:23.758
We're obviously not weirdoes!

09:25.295 --> 09:26.494
See, Brian? Told ya.

09:26.530 --> 09:28.430
We're going to be home
in no time.

09:28.465 --> 09:29.465
Hi there, folks.

09:29.499 --> 09:31.466
Hand over the turkey.
What?!

09:31.501 --> 09:33.568
I can't go back to my wife
without a turkey!

09:33.603 --> 09:34.736
Oh, yeah?

09:34.771 --> 09:36.604
Bet that thing's
not even loaded.

09:36.640 --> 09:40.241
You just used
your last bullet.

09:40.277 --> 09:42.711
Running on empty now.

09:42.746 --> 09:45.547
Brian, give him the turkey.

09:53.023 --> 09:55.957
Okay, buddy, you ready to
test out those hosting skills?

09:55.992 --> 09:58.426
Now go wow your guests
with conversation.

09:59.863 --> 10:01.262
Hi, Grandma.

10:01.298 --> 10:03.998
I got some down-there
hair now-- want to see?

10:04.034 --> 10:05.767
Uh, I-I...

10:05.802 --> 10:08.636
I should check if your mother
needs help in the kitchen.

10:08.672 --> 10:12.240
Sometimes I pluck them
because I deserve pain.

10:17.581 --> 10:19.614
Cut! No. Stop.

10:19.649 --> 10:21.116
I'm sorry! I panicked!

10:21.151 --> 10:23.284
It's all right. It's okay.
Don't worry, Chris.

10:23.320 --> 10:25.653
You can't always get things
right on the first try.

10:25.689 --> 10:28.490
Just look at Snoopy's
original happy dance.

10:30.527 --> 10:33.762
Hey, you having
a good time tonight?

10:35.632 --> 10:37.398
Oh, yeah.

10:41.538 --> 10:42.971
Can't believe
we got robbed.

10:43.006 --> 10:44.606
Yeah, but can we just
talk for a second

10:44.641 --> 10:47.509
about how brave I was when
we walked past that cemetery?

10:47.544 --> 10:50.211
Peter, do you not see that we
are completely screwed here?

10:50.247 --> 10:51.813
And it's all
thanks to you!

10:51.848 --> 10:54.315
You drove my car into a lake,
you almost let me drown,

10:54.351 --> 10:56.818
you got us thrown off a bus,
you broke our bike,

10:56.853 --> 10:58.386
and now you've gotten
our turkey stolen

10:58.421 --> 10:59.654
and Thanksgiving
is ruined

10:59.689 --> 11:00.955
and we don't have
any transportation

11:00.991 --> 11:02.657
and we're still
miles from home!

11:02.692 --> 11:05.093
You're starting to get
black gums like an older dog.

11:05.128 --> 11:07.088
You know what? You know what?
Maybe it's my fault.

11:07.097 --> 11:08.897
I forgot, I'm talking
to a complete idiot.

11:08.932 --> 11:10.365
You are so stupid!

11:10.400 --> 11:11.400
Oh, yeah?

11:11.401 --> 11:12.834
Well, if I'm so stupid,

11:12.869 --> 11:15.537
then how did I manage to
frame you for eating the turkey?

11:15.572 --> 11:17.205
What?!
Yeah!

11:17.240 --> 11:19.240
Didn't you notice you were
passed out in all those photos?

11:19.276 --> 11:20.341
You didn't eat any of it.

11:20.377 --> 11:21.776
I just posed you like that

11:21.812 --> 11:23.545
because I didn't want
to take all the blame.

11:23.580 --> 11:26.114
You son of a bitch!
How could you do that to me?

11:26.149 --> 11:27.315
You're a dog, Brian.

11:27.350 --> 11:29.083
I can throw you
off a bridge,

11:29.119 --> 11:31.719
and as long as I don't hit
a person on a boat, it's okay.

11:31.755 --> 11:33.288
Screw this. I am done!

11:33.323 --> 11:35.323
This isn't even my problem,
it's your problem.

11:35.358 --> 11:36.791
You know what, Peter?

11:36.827 --> 11:38.860
You've got no turkey,
and now you've got no friend.

11:38.895 --> 11:40.395
Good-bye!

11:40.430 --> 11:42.297
W-Wait-- Brian, wait!

11:43.733 --> 11:47.735
♪ Now let's watch
a whole bunch of ads. ♪

11:51.153 --> 11:52.486
Nice Thanksgiving.

11:52.521 --> 11:54.821
I don't know why I ever listen
to that jerk.

11:54.857 --> 11:56.156
What?

11:56.191 --> 11:58.031
Home is this way;
we're both just walking home.

11:58.060 --> 11:59.393
Leave me alone!

11:59.428 --> 12:01.928
No way. We're a team, Brian,
whether you like it or not.

12:01.964 --> 12:03.130
Just like almond butter

12:03.165 --> 12:05.499
and no sugar added
fruit preserves.

12:05.534 --> 12:06.667
Who's hungry?

12:06.702 --> 12:08.468
We are!

12:08.504 --> 12:11.171
<i>Hey, kids, would you like
a terrible healthy sandwich?</i>

12:11.206 --> 12:12.472
No.

12:12.508 --> 12:15.042
<i>Too bad, because
your recently divorced mom</i>

12:15.077 --> 12:17.778
<i>has a crush on her trainer,
and he eats like this,</i>

12:17.813 --> 12:19.646
<i>so now you have to, too.</i>

12:19.682 --> 12:22.382
<i>Almond butter and no sugar
added fruit preserves--</i>

12:22.418 --> 12:23.850
<i>just like PB and J,</i>

12:23.886 --> 12:26.286
<i>but with more
of your mom railing this guy.</i>

12:26.322 --> 12:28.789
I named myself Kaya!

12:28.824 --> 12:30.223
We stopped being a team

12:30.259 --> 12:32.292
when you framed me for eating
that turkey with you.

12:32.328 --> 12:34.594
Brian, maybe you should be
a little less mad at me

12:34.630 --> 12:36.263
and a little more mad
at the guys

12:36.298 --> 12:37.798
growing mustaches
for this month.

12:37.833 --> 12:39.099
Hey, don't mock
Mo-vember.

12:39.134 --> 12:40.767
Last year, I raised
eight dollars

12:40.803 --> 12:42.269
and got on
a BuzzFeed listicle.

12:42.304 --> 12:44.338
No! You use real words!

12:44.373 --> 12:46.773
Internet stuff
is not real words.

12:46.809 --> 12:48.842
Hey, look!

12:51.113 --> 12:52.245
There's our answer.

12:52.281 --> 12:54.247
We break into the zoo,
steal a turkey,

12:54.283 --> 12:55.916
bring it home, we're heroes.

12:56.952 --> 12:58.151
Peter, stop it!

12:58.187 --> 12:59.387
You're gonna
get yourself hurt.

12:59.421 --> 13:00.654
Sorry, can't hear you.

13:00.689 --> 13:02.389
Too busy saving
our family's Thanksgiving.

13:02.424 --> 13:04.157
Damn it.

13:04.193 --> 13:05.258
This is idiotic.

13:05.294 --> 13:06.860
You're never gonna find
a turkey in there.

13:06.895 --> 13:08.128
Oh, I'll find one.

13:08.163 --> 13:09.496
I mean, you're
looking at the guy

13:09.531 --> 13:11.064
who found the
Fountain of Youth.

13:13.936 --> 13:17.304
It's very far
away from here!

13:22.344 --> 13:23.777
Hey, Lois,
thanks for letting Kevin

13:23.812 --> 13:25.379
bring his girlfriend
this year.

13:25.414 --> 13:27.848
And I hope it's not awkward
that she's a little person

13:27.883 --> 13:29.649
and they viciously fight
all the time.

13:29.685 --> 13:32.352
<i>Why do we have to spend every
holiday with your family?</i>

13:32.388 --> 13:34.488
Shut up!
I'm a full-size person!

13:34.523 --> 13:35.889
I make the decisions!

13:35.924 --> 13:37.724
Don't you worry.
This'll quickly turn

13:37.760 --> 13:40.093
into rough,
front-yard, makeup sex.

13:40.129 --> 13:42.896
All this fighting is
making me so damn hot.

13:46.402 --> 13:47.667
Oh, my God.

13:47.703 --> 13:50.170
It looks like he's
chalking a pool cue.

13:50.205 --> 13:51.338
Hey, scoot over.

13:51.373 --> 13:52.739
As the oldest guy here,

13:52.775 --> 13:54.674
it's my duty to take
an open mouth nap

13:54.710 --> 13:56.009
in the middle of the room.

14:05.921 --> 14:07.287
God, look at my mom.

14:07.322 --> 14:09.022
Dinner should've been served
half an hour ago.

14:09.057 --> 14:11.057
She's clearly stalling
for time.

14:11.093 --> 14:12.225
Okay, everybody.

14:12.261 --> 14:14.494
Dinner's gonna be ready
very soon.

14:14.530 --> 14:16.029
Uh, what?

14:16.064 --> 14:17.731
Um, oh, good.

14:17.766 --> 14:19.299
But before we get started,

14:19.334 --> 14:22.536
I thought we could all take
turns telling a long story

14:22.571 --> 14:25.238
about how things aren't
the way they used to be.

14:25.274 --> 14:27.307
Daddy, would you care
to start?

14:27.342 --> 14:28.408
You bet I would.

14:28.444 --> 14:29.609
Too much candy!

14:29.645 --> 14:30.811
Too much candy?

14:30.846 --> 14:32.612
What do you mean,
too much candy?

14:32.648 --> 14:33.814
There's too much candy!

14:33.849 --> 14:35.449
There used to be four candies.

14:35.484 --> 14:38.151
Bulls-eyes, Yahoos,
Sweet Yarn and cigarettes.

14:38.187 --> 14:39.553
Now I go into a store,

14:39.588 --> 14:41.121
I don't know whether
I'm coming or going!

14:41.156 --> 14:42.522
Is there anything else?

14:42.558 --> 14:45.225
Why don't ballplayers wear
giant woolen shirts anymore?

14:45.260 --> 14:46.793
What's wrong with wool?

14:46.829 --> 14:48.161
It was a perfect fabric.

14:48.197 --> 14:50.397
You go to the ballpark,
get your bag of Bulls-eyes

14:50.432 --> 14:53.233
and watch Hack Wilson round
the bases in a big wool shirt.

14:53.268 --> 14:55.735
I once saw Hack hit a ball
out of the infield.

14:55.771 --> 14:57.704
I still remember
the thud of the bat

14:57.739 --> 14:59.239
and the whoosh of the wool.

14:59.274 --> 15:02.676
I wish things were still heavy.

15:02.711 --> 15:04.211
Oh, the rails are
off this thing.

15:04.246 --> 15:06.079
All right, Chris,
this is where you, as host,

15:06.114 --> 15:07.481
need to step in and...

15:07.516 --> 15:10.150
Chris? Chris?

15:11.420 --> 15:13.386
What the hell?
Are you drunk?

15:13.422 --> 15:15.155
I couldn't handle
the pressure, Stewie.

15:15.190 --> 15:18.458
We Irish,
we have a deep sadness.

15:18.494 --> 15:20.827
Oh, come on, get up!
They need you down there.

15:20.863 --> 15:24.998
♪ Too-Ra-loo-Ra-loo-ral. ♪

15:32.341 --> 15:33.707
All right, there they are.

15:33.742 --> 15:36.109
I'm going in and getting
us a turkey, Brian.

15:40.449 --> 15:42.916
Hey, buddy, you want
to come to my house

15:42.951 --> 15:45.218
so my wife can cook you wrong?

15:45.254 --> 15:46.953
Ah, damn it!

15:48.357 --> 15:50.123
Peter, this is never gonna work.

15:50.158 --> 15:51.678
All right,
just leave the turkey alone.

15:51.693 --> 15:52.893
The poor thing is... Aah! Aah!

15:52.928 --> 15:54.194
What the hell?!
Knock it off!

15:54.229 --> 15:56.062
Ow! Damn it, I'm gonna
kill you, you dick!

15:56.098 --> 15:58.565
Quick, Brian,
it's getting away!

16:12.047 --> 16:14.681
Where'd he go?

16:16.285 --> 16:18.151
He's not in here.

16:18.186 --> 16:20.020
Over there!

16:52.421 --> 16:53.753
Oh, crap.

16:53.789 --> 16:55.121
Easy there.

16:55.157 --> 16:57.123
Hey, it's Thanksgiving.

16:57.159 --> 16:58.592
Shouldn't you be in Detroit

16:58.627 --> 17:00.126
losing a football game
right now?

17:06.101 --> 17:07.867
Brian, up here!

17:13.775 --> 17:14.908
Oh, my God.

17:14.943 --> 17:16.876
Thank you, Peter.
Thank you so much!

17:16.912 --> 17:18.945
Hey, you're welcome, buddy.

17:18.981 --> 17:20.180
You...

17:20.215 --> 17:21.715
You saved my life.

17:21.750 --> 17:22.916
Of course I did.

17:22.951 --> 17:24.618
You're my best friend.

17:24.653 --> 17:25.919
Hey, listen, I'm-I'm...

17:25.954 --> 17:27.954
I'm sorry I messed
everything up today.

17:27.990 --> 17:29.956
It's okay.

17:29.992 --> 17:31.992
I guess I've been
kind of a jerk, too.

17:32.027 --> 17:33.994
I'm sorry I yelled at you.

17:34.029 --> 17:35.495
Ah, I deserved it.

17:35.530 --> 17:38.064
I mean, for God's sake,
I sank your car in a lake.

17:38.100 --> 17:40.533
And I broke
this guy's neck just now.

17:42.337 --> 17:43.503
Yeesh.

17:43.538 --> 17:45.839
But, hey, we cut the legs
off him and dye him brown,

17:45.874 --> 17:47.273
we got ourselves
a turkey, right?

17:47.309 --> 17:49.142
No. We've come this far.

17:49.177 --> 17:51.144
Let's do it right.

17:53.815 --> 17:56.716
Hey, you got a tiny head
and a big body.

17:56.752 --> 17:58.752
What if I switched that?

17:59.955 --> 18:01.054
Gotcha!

18:01.089 --> 18:02.489
All right, we did it!

18:02.524 --> 18:03.757
We got ourselves a turkey.

18:03.792 --> 18:04.991
Yeah, but what
time is it?

18:05.027 --> 18:06.667
I mean, dinner has to
have started by now.

18:06.695 --> 18:08.094
We're never gonna make
it home on foot.

18:08.130 --> 18:10.130
Maybe we don't have to.

18:15.303 --> 18:16.836
We're now arriving in Quahog.

18:16.872 --> 18:19.272
Up on the right are the people
with the awesome trampoline,

18:19.307 --> 18:21.241
but they don't let me
on it no more,

18:21.276 --> 18:23.677
'cause I bounced a kid
onto the house.

18:25.380 --> 18:27.280
There were no
squeezable condiments.

18:27.315 --> 18:28.748
Ketchup came in a can.

18:28.784 --> 18:31.785
And, Daddy, what about the pants
that kids today are wearing?

18:31.820 --> 18:33.820
Are they properly sized?

18:33.855 --> 18:35.155
Are we gonna eat soon?

18:35.190 --> 18:36.389
I have an interesting factoid

18:36.425 --> 18:38.458
about what makes you
sleepy afterwards.

18:38.493 --> 18:40.493
Yeah, the hell with this.
I'm starving.

18:41.963 --> 18:44.931
Okay, I guess we should eat.

18:47.369 --> 18:49.369
Well, obviously
Peter's not here.

18:49.404 --> 18:51.638
So it's fallen to me
to take up the mantle.

18:51.673 --> 18:54.140
Now, I wasn't planning on
doing this today,

18:54.176 --> 18:57.777
but when I look around at all
of these open, loving faces

18:57.813 --> 18:59.412
or friends and family,

18:59.448 --> 19:01.915
I am comfortable enough
to finally say

19:01.950 --> 19:05.251
that I am a proud,
unashamed, active...

19:05.287 --> 19:08.388
Lois, we're home
and Thanksgiving is saved!

19:08.423 --> 19:09.689
Kidding!

19:09.725 --> 19:11.691
Oh, my God, where the
hell have you been?

19:11.727 --> 19:13.560
And what are you doing
with a live turkey?!

19:13.595 --> 19:16.329
A live turkey
who loves Rollerblading.

19:18.633 --> 19:19.999
Our dog drew that.

19:20.035 --> 19:22.168
Peter, we can't eat
a live turkey.

19:22.204 --> 19:24.771
Look, Lois, I still got time
to make this right.

19:24.806 --> 19:25.905
And I'm gonna.

19:25.941 --> 19:28.608
Hand me a nine iron
and show me to the backyard.

19:30.445 --> 19:33.513
Well, buddy, I guess this is it.

19:44.626 --> 19:46.526
Aah! Aah!

19:46.561 --> 19:48.628
Wow, I-I...

19:48.663 --> 19:50.630
I read that look wrong.

19:50.665 --> 19:52.432
Ah, geez, I'm sorry.

19:52.467 --> 19:54.067
I wish you didn't have to die,

19:54.102 --> 19:56.436
but a bunch of white people
put on sweaters.

20:01.877 --> 20:03.743
I couldn't do it.
What?

20:03.779 --> 20:05.111
I'm sorry, Lois.

20:05.147 --> 20:06.827
I know you wanted the
perfect Thanksgiving,

20:06.848 --> 20:08.782
and I know I screwed
that all up for you,

20:08.817 --> 20:10.416
but when you
think about it,

20:10.452 --> 20:13.019
isn't this holiday about
being with people you love?

20:13.054 --> 20:15.421
I mean, does it really matter
what we eat?

20:15.457 --> 20:17.390
What matters
is we're all together.

20:17.425 --> 20:19.592
Family and friends.

20:19.628 --> 20:21.795
And one new friend.

20:21.830 --> 20:24.330
Oh, Peter, that's beautiful.

20:24.366 --> 20:27.200
Lois, can the turkey please
join us for dinner?

20:27.235 --> 20:30.270
Not as the meal,
but as our guest?

20:30.305 --> 20:32.071
Of course he can.

20:32.107 --> 20:33.773
Happy Thanksgiving, everyone.

20:35.877 --> 20:38.778
The man of the house

20:38.814 --> 20:41.481
killed a turkey
for Thanksgiving!

20:42.851 --> 20:44.717
Well, looks like we're
having turkey after all.

20:46.161 --> 20:51.161
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru

20:51.162 --> 20:53.322
<i>Four years later, me and Lois
divorced and Stewie died.</i>

20:54.881 --> 20:56.847
<i>Gobble, gobble!</i>